    "intro_html":  "Rogan josh is a Kashmiri dish, and the authentic version does something almost no other Indian curry does: it uses no onions and no tomatoes at all. The deep red color comes from Kashmiri chiles, which are more about pigment than punishment. The body comes from yogurt, whisked in slowly so it does not split, and the perfume comes from dried ginger and fennel. It is a short list of ingredients doing very precise work. Each serving runs \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
